<title>FRANCE: Air France Paris cargo share down Q1 97.</title>
<headline>Air France Paris cargo share down Q1 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France's share of global air cargo tonnage handled at the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in the first quarter of 1997 decreased on 1996 as a whole, Aeroport de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The carrier's share of ADP's global cargo tonnage in January-March 1997, totalling 273,110 tonnes, was 54.5 percent compared to 55.5 percent in calendar 1996.</p>
<p>The top 10 cargo-handling airlines at the ADP airports by tonnage share in the first three months of this year, together with 1996 full-year tonnage share, were as follows:</p>
<p>		     Jan-Mar 1997	 1996 (full year)</p>
<p>Air France	   54.5 percent	    55.5</p>
<p>Federal Express     7.4			 6.8</p>
<p>Air France Europe (ex-Air Inter)</p>
<p>			  2.9			 3.8</p>
<p>American Airlines   2.3			 2.0</p>
<p>Air Canada	    2.2			 1.7</p>
<p>L'Aeropostale	 1.8			 1.9</p>
<p>Japan Airlines	1.7			 1.6</p>
<p>United Airlines     1.6			 1.3</p>
<p>Air Outre Mer (AOM) 1.6			 N.A.</p>
<p>Cathay Pacific	1.5			 1.8</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
